w off vet in return of  the jedi the sarlacc of the great pit of  carcoon  appeared to have swallowed him up  looking closely the jet pack in the  teaser trailer appears to have the same  muted orange and blue green color scheme  as the one boba fett wore  in the sixth installment of the  skywalker saga especially taking into  consideration the damage it likely  endured from the sarlacc  and all the dust that's coating it the  question many have about this possible  glimpse of boba fett's pack is he will  be wearing it  if it's not the man himself perhaps  someone somehow came across the  undigested jet pack in the desert  and kept it for themselves it could be  jarring but there are reports that  someone new will take up fed's iconic  garb in the mandalorian  at least for a time back in may 2020 the  news broke that deadwood star timothy  oliphant would join the castle the  mandalorian season 2  in an undisclosed role an anonymous  inside source allegedly told the folks  at slash film that olly  fund was spotted on set in fed's  distinctive gear suggesting that whoever  his character is he will take ownership  of the discarded armor  and masquerade as a bounty hunter  there's actually precedent for this in  the current star wars canon as chuck  wendig's novel aftermath introduces  kobanth  a tatooine sheriff who buys the salvaged  outfit from some jawas  if fett is actually alive like he was in  the now non-canonical star wars expanded  universe of books  and other media maybe he'll work  alongside dinjarin to recover his  missing gear  or maybe jaren will take it upon himself  to put a stop to olefin's character  making a mockery of mandalorian armor  time will tell  from the moment he first appeared in the  star wars holiday special back in 1978  fans became instantly enamored with the  mysterious bounty hunter  his live-action appearances in both the  empire strikes back  and return of the jedi only increased  their fascination despite his limited  screen time  